{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: reordered the existing parameter prior sampling statements for `a`, `b`, and `sigma` so that each parameter is observed by its built-in prior before being used to compute `y_pred` or the likelihood. This preserves the same posterior/log density because Stan sampling statements add to the log density commutatively. The data file is unchanged.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int N;
  vector[N] x;
  vector[N] y;
}
parameters {
  vector<lower=0>[2] a;
  positive_ordered[2] b;
  real<lower=0> sigma;
}
model {
  vector[N] y_pred;
  a ~ normal(0, 1);
  b ~ normal(0, 1);
  sigma ~ normal(0, 1);
  y_pred = a[1] * exp(-b[1] * x) + a[2] * exp(-b[2] * x);
  y ~ lognormal(log(y_pred), sigma);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":4,"x":[2.686108490672436,4.553499350608059,2.536038879710432,5.232771690087374],"y":[4.0,4.0,4.0,4.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
